From: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/pm: use the VBIOS trained UCLK levels on Apple Navi boards

The Radeon Pro 5300M and 5500M of the MacBookPro16,1 (Navi 14) hang the
SMU as soon as UCLK may switch under DPM auto, low or a free pp_dpm_mclk.
The SMU then answers no message, metrics reads fail and the T2 watchdog
resets the machine.

The SMU runs UCLK level L on UMC p-state register set 3 - L, which the
boot firmware trained at the frequencies umc_info v3.3 lists. On these
boards the sets were trained at 95, 496, 598 and 736 MHz, while the
pptable lists 95, 496, 736 and 750 MHz. A switch into level 2 runs 736
MHz on a set trained at 598 MHz and never completes. PC Navi 10 and
Navi 14 VBIOS images list the same frequencies in both tables.

Replace the UCLK levels of Apple boards with the trained frequencies
and lower the DC mode UCLK maximum to the top one. This changes nothing
where both tables already match. It replaces the 740 MHz UCLK cap,
which kept level 3 off and left the mistrained level 2 as the top.

Reported with this table uploaded through pp_table on two 5300M and one
5500M: all four UCLK levels used under DPM auto and real load, no SMU
errors, suspend and resume fine.

Signed-off-by: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu11/navi10_ppt.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu11/navi10_ppt.c
@@ -468,6 +468,53 @@ static int navi10_store_powerplay_table(struct smu_context *smu)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Apple's VBIOS trains the UMC p-state register sets of the MacBookPro16,1
+ * Navi 14 at other frequencies than its pptable lists for UCLK. The SMU runs
+ * UCLK level L on set NUM_UCLK_DPM_LEVELS - 1 - L, and a switch into a level
+ * whose set was trained at another frequency never completes and leaves the
+ * SMU unresponsive. umc_info v3.3 lists the frequency each set was trained at.
+ * Use those as the UCLK levels, which changes nothing where they already match.
+ */
+static void navi10_apple_fix_uclk_levels(struct smu_context *smu)
+{
+	struct amdgpu_device *adev = smu->adev;
+	PPTable_t *pptable = smu->smu_table.driver_pptable;
+	struct atom_umc_info_v3_3 *umc_info;
+	uint16_t trained[NUM_UCLK_DPM_LEVELS];
+	uint16_t size;
+	uint8_t frev, crev;
+	int index, i;
+
+	if (adev->pdev->subsystem_vendor != PCI_VENDOR_ID_APPLE ||
+	    pptable->DpmDescriptor[PPCLK_UCLK].NumDiscreteLevels != NUM_UCLK_DPM_LEVELS)
+		return;
+
+	index = get_index_into_master_table(atom_master_list_of_data_tables_v2_1,
+					    umc_info);
+	if (amdgpu_atombios_get_data_table(adev, index, &size, &frev, &crev,
+					   (uint8_t **)&umc_info) ||
+	    frev != 3 || crev != 3 || size < sizeof(*umc_info))
+		return;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < NUM_UCLK_DPM_LEVELS; i++) {
+		trained[i] = le32_to_cpu(umc_info->pstate_uclk_10khz[MAX_UCLK_DPM_LEVEL - i]) / 100;
+		if (!trained[i] || (i && trained[i] <= trained[i - 1]))
+			return;
+	}
+
+	for (i = 0; i < NUM_UCLK_DPM_LEVELS; i++) {
+		if (pptable->FreqTableUclk[i] == trained[i])
+			continue;
+		dev_info(adev->dev, "UCLK level %d: %u MHz -> %u MHz, as trained by the VBIOS\n",
+			 i, pptable->FreqTableUclk[i], trained[i]);
+		pptable->FreqTableUclk[i] = trained[i];
+	}
+
+	pptable->DcModeMaxFreq[PPCLK_UCLK] = min(pptable->DcModeMaxFreq[PPCLK_UCLK],
+						 trained[MAX_UCLK_DPM_LEVEL]);
+}
+
 static int navi10_setup_pptable(struct smu_context *smu)
 {
 	int ret = 0;
@@ -480,6 +527,8 @@ static int navi10_setup_pptable(struct smu_context *smu)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	navi10_apple_fix_uclk_levels(smu);
+
 	ret = navi10_append_powerplay_table(smu);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
